  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "RGL-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-real-gram-lift",
      "title": "Compact isometries lifting a regular Gram fibre at a real place",
      "statement": "For a nonsingular complex Hermitian form and a fixed ordered frame X with invertible Gram matrix T, there is a compact family of unitary maps whose images of X cover all tuples of Gram matrix T in any prescribed compact set.",
      "hypotheses": "One real completion of the totally real base, complex conjugation on the coefficient field, finite dimension, an invertible Hermitian form and a nonsingular fixed Gram matrix. The compact set lies in the ordinary topology of the tuple space. The signature can be indefinite.",
      "correspondence": "The two explicit unitary corrections and the induction are the complex-place specialization of the recorded algebraic construction. The lower bound on the denominator for one of the two signs, the closed finite cover and the example are proved here. The general adelic supplier proves transitivity on the closed fibre. The passage explains the Baire argument that opens the orbit map for the locally compact second-countable group and the finite subcover that lifts compact sets. The outgoing links identify the real-place component of the adelic input, without asserting a literal invocation of a separately named real-place lemma.",
      "dependencies": [],
